      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "WHISPER'S BOY (7) turned in a solid run last start over 342m at this track finishing 4th and beaten only 4.5 lengths (20.13). Solid beginner and with a good start should have clear running out wide. Worth another chance. REGAL MACK (2) was prominent early from the tricky draw and did a fair job to be beaten 3.5 lengths into third (20.07) at this track in a Maiden over 342m. Speedy beginner who should be prominent early on from an inside box. Can feature again. JUST ON FIRE (8) has been beaten for early speed lately, last time finishing fourth (23.29) in a Maiden at Gawler. Has never been out of the money in five starts this distance. Expected to give a good account. REDEEMER LEE (1) is worth another chance despite missing the top-three here most recently.",
